`13` after the later base-three LCM factor is included.  This exact
certificate is distinct from Rhin's printed exponent `13.3`. -/
theorem rhinRelaxedRateCertificate :
    (72 : ℚ) * ((3 : ℚ) * (239 / 1000)) ^ 13 < 1 ∧
      (13 : ℚ) ≤ 133 / 10 := by
  norm_num

